The Notes app is a tool I use nearly every day. I think my habit of using it grew out of the way my mom taught me to stay organized in school. 
She always encouraged us to keep a planner, and over time, my phone became the place where I could quickly write down anything I didn’t want to forget.
I use Notes for to-do lists, reminders, ideas, and thoughts that I want to return to later, and I like that everything is accessible from both my phone and laptop. 
I currently have 635 notes, with my oldest dating back to 2015, which made me realize how long this app has been part of my life. 
If Notes did not exist, I would probably return to using a physical planner or carry a small notebook, although it would be harder to keep everything organized and 
accessible in one place.
